{
  "_comment": [
    "Ground truth for the meshbench ClickHouse benchmark dataset, captured at",
    "source. These are FIXED EXPECTATIONS, not re-measurements: the dataset is",
    "generated with zero rand() and every column derived from",
    "cityHash64(number, k), so it regenerates byte-identically from",
    "bench/make-dataset.sh alone. Any e2e parity miss against these numbers is a",
    "pipeline defect, never dataset drift.",
    "",
    "scaled_amount_sum is round(sum(amount)*100) as specified. Because ClickHouse",
    "sums float64 in parallel and float addition is not associative, that form is",
    "in principle order-sensitive, so scaled_amount_sum_exact_int computes the",
    "same quantity with order-independent integer arithmetic",
    "(sum(toInt64(round(amount*100)))). The two agreed exactly and were stable",
    "across 3 consecutive reps on both tables at capture time; the integer form is",
    "the authority if they ever diverge."
  ],
